  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100888,
      "id": "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a",
      "title": "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1fdec905-581f-5326-98ae-4aeb54c34bc3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 6 e^{\\frac{y}{2}},\\qquad 4 x - 4>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 4 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{4}{4 x - 4}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 4 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 4 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot\\frac{4}{4 x - 4} \\\\ &=- \\frac{8}{4 x - 4} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{4 x - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 4 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{8}{4 x - 4}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 6 e^{\\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{8}{4 x - 4} &\\overset{?}{=}-6e^{-(- 2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 4 \\right)})/(-2)} \\\\ - \\frac{8}{4 x - 4} &\\overset{?}{=}-6e^{-\\ln(4 x - 4)} \\\\ - \\frac{8}{4 x - 4} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{3}{2 x - 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 4 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b149f631-6f88-5d77-b748-4a9fc75bf77a",
